A||N||1||wardog85GT||Questions about 3.1 I just bought||||5||
Z||000000||wardog85GT||05-06-2001||08:08 PM||||I would like to install the 3.1 into my 85 GT. The engine came from a '90 lumina. What would be the best thing to do? Should I just Install the intake plenums on the 3.1 or should I just take the bottom end out and put it in the 2.8 block. I would really like to use the aluminum heads if they produce more HP.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT GT 87||05-06-2001||10:19 PM||||You can use the alum. heads but they will be a hassle. First you have to use the 3.1 intake cause the 2.8 won't fit the head ports. And that means it points to the passenger side , hard to mount aircleaner and throtle cablr .  The alum. heads don't like the high temp's in the fiero engine compartment.  You can't use the stock distr. you have to use the coil pac's from the 3.1.  I am building a 3.1 with crank rods and "new clean up bore" pistons from a 3.1 in my 2.8 block. I will be useing the iron heads with a port job and etc. The stager valves in the alum. head flow better but not worth the trouble................. Steve<p>[This message has been edited by GT GT 87 (edited 05-06-2001).]||||reg||1
